From 128b38ac49fec3eff83cf86dc1bde32340767774 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hhdy <103477680+hhdy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:48:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] regulator: add boot time proxy consumer support

Port the Qualcomm boot time regulator proxy consumer helper onto the pinned
ACK 6.18.33 tree so that qcom,proxy-consumer-* requests can be expressed by
a board DTS again. ACK currently has neither the source file, the Kconfig
symbol, the Makefile entry, nor the regulator core hook.

The helper is invoked from regulator_register() and regulator_unregister().
It resolves the "proxy" supply on the device that registers the regulator
(the PMIC group node) while reading qcom,proxy-consumer-enable,
qcom,proxy-consumer-current and qcom,proxy-consumer-voltage from the
regulator child node (config->of_node). That split matches the HOS4.3
topology, where proxy-supply sits on the provider group and the request
flags sit on the regulator child, so no phandle is reinterpreted here.

All requests are withdrawn once at late_initcall_sync. A single regulator
teardown withdraws only its own request through the regulator_dev
back-pointer, and the bulk removal clears that pointer, so the bulk path
and a per-regulator unregister can never act on the same consumer twice.
Every partially applied request is unwound in reverse order on failure.

The Kconfig symbol is placed after the core objects in the Makefile so that
the late_initcall_sync order stays core-first, proxy-second.

Signed-off-by: hhdy <103477680+hhdy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/regulator/Kconfig                |  12 +
 drivers/regulator/Makefile               |   1 +
 drivers/regulator/core.c                 |   5 +
 drivers/regulator/proxy-consumer.c       | 316 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/regulator/driver.h         |   3 +-
 include/linux/regulator/proxy-consumer.h |  41 +++
 6 files changed, 377 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/regulator/proxy-consumer.c
 create mode 100644 include/linux/regulator/proxy-consumer.h

diff --git a/drivers/regulator/Kconfig b/drivers/regulator/Kconfig
index d84f3d054c59..1eb68d402fe2 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/regulator/Kconfig
@@ -56,6 +56,18 @@ config REGULATOR_USERSPACE_CONSUMER
 
 	  If unsure, say no.
 
+config REGULATOR_PROXY_CONSUMER
+	bool "Boot time regulator proxy consumer support"
+	help
+	  This driver provides support for boot time regulator proxy requests.
+	  It can enforce a specified voltage range, set a minimum current,
+	  and/or keep a regulator enabled.  It is needed in circumstances where
+	  reducing one or more of these three quantities will cause hardware to
+	  stop working if performed before the driver managing the hardware has
+	  probed.
+
+	  If unsure, say no.
+
 config REGULATOR_NETLINK_EVENTS
 	bool "Enable support for receiving regulator events via netlink"
 	depends on NET
